lesson k-a-repeat v=1 format=teach grade=0 unit=8 subject=coding levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Do it again: a repeat"
  goal "Do a pattern of claps and stamps several times, and read a repeat block that says how many times to do what is inside it."

  look {
    scene 30x10 {
      row top at=canvas(1, 0) space=1 align=start {
        blocks bl code=["repeat 3", "  jump"] words=false numbers=false
        stage st cols=5 col=2 who=rabbit code=["repeat 3", "  jump"] flag=false upto=-1
      }
    }
    say """
      The orange block is a repeat. It holds a jump and says three, so the rabbit jumps three times.
      Clap, clap, stamp done again and again is a repeat too. A repeat saves writing the same block
      over and over.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked k.clap-repeat n=2 level=medium
    }
    practice k.clap-repeat count=2 seed=2 easy-count=1
    practice k.jumps-in-repeat count=3 seed=3 easy-count=2 hard-count=2
    practice k.repeat-hops count=2 seed=4
    show k.pattern-next c=6 easy-c=4 hard-c=7
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show k.shorter-with-repeat
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show k.repeat-pattern k=0 hard-k=1
  }
  remember {
    say "A repeat does what is inside it again and again, as many times as it says."
  }

  grown-ups """
    Read each question aloud and do the claps and stamps together; the body learns a loop before
    the page does. If the child is stuck on the repeat block, put the same toy through the same
    move three times and count. Off the page, make up a clapping pattern and repeat it, then let
    the child say what repeats and how many times. Japan, 幼稚園教育要領 (kindergarten guidelines),
    環境, 内容 (7), as in the first coding lesson.
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level two rounds of claps are worked in the teacher's pen first, the repeats say two or three, and the pattern to find is clap, stamp."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the repeats say four or five, the rabbit hops two squares each time, and the pattern to find is clap, clap, stamp."
  }
}
